            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 10 changed paths in full. The package is a pure domain package: it reads no files, runs no git, and has no network or secret handling.",
              "CheckFeature restricts a feature to ASCII alphanumerics plus '.', '_' and '-', requires a leading alphanumeric, forbids '..', and caps length at 100 bytes. This blocks traversal, separators, absolute paths and option-like names before ResultPath joins the feature into a path (engine/review/names.go).",
              "CheckRev refuses empty revisions, a leading '-' (which git would read as an option such as --output), and control characters including NUL and DEL (engine/review/names.go).",
              "NewCandidate requires full lowercase hex object names of equal length, so Short() slicing the first 12 characters of the head cannot panic on a candidate it built. A zero Candidate would panic in Short, but that is an out-of-domain value.",
              "NextNumber caps launch numbers at 9 digits and rejects leading zeros, so Atoi cannot overflow. ResultName and WorktreePath use only validated hex and fixed strings.",
              "EncodeResult validates the reply with json.Valid before embedding it as a RawMessage, so the stored file is always valid JSON. HTML escaping is disabled only for readability of a file written to disk, not for HTML output, so it creates no injection exposure.",
              "No new dependencies were added and no secrets appear. The only edit outside the new package is the architecture ring registration for the review package, which is a test-file change.",
              "No exploitable or reachable risk was found in this candidate."
            ]
          }
        }
